<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Height is fixed by design. The card shows exactly one account — header,
  account row, flow row, action pills — so there is no list to stretch and
  nothing useful for a vertical resize to do.

  That is what retires the two resize bugs the old list version had: a blank
  gap opening below a short account list, and shrinking clipping a row's
  middle. Both came from a defaultWeight()-stretched LazyColumn absorbing
  whatever height the launcher allocated. Declaring the widget
  horizontally-resizable only, at a height matching its actual content,
  removes the condition rather than compensating for it.

  The numbers below are load-bearing, and getting them too small clips
  content rather than merely looking off. Measured content height is ~190dp:

    padding 14*2 = 28   header 22   gap 8   account row 36
    gap 8 + divider 1 + gap 8       flow row ~31
    gap 8                           pills 36

  targetCellHeight="3" was tried first and starved it — on a 1080x2400
  device three cells came out around 150dp, so the weighted body was
  squeezed and the Income/Expense/Transfers values were clipped away
  entirely behind the pills. Four cells lands near 200dp, just above the
  content, which is what this needs.

  minResizeHeight/minHeight are the real guarantee: they are a hard floor
  for placement, so even a launcher that ignores targetCellHeight cannot
  size this below its own content.

  Vertical resize stays ENABLED, but bracketed to 200-230dp. Disabling it
  outright was tried and is worse: a widget already placed at an older,
  shorter size keeps that size across an app update, and with vertical
  resize off the user has no way to drag it taller — they have to delete
  and re-add it. The bracket is what actually prevents the two old bugs
  (it cannot shrink below its content, nor stretch far enough to open a
  meaningful gap), so the escape hatch costs nothing.
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:minWidth="250dp"
    android:minHeight="200dp"
    android:targetCellWidth="4"
    android:targetCellHeight="4"
    android:minResizeWidth="250dp"
    android:minResizeHeight="200dp"
    android:maxResizeHeight="230dp"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/glance_default_loading_layout"
    android:previewImage="@drawable/preview_accounts"
    android:widgetFeatures="reconfigurable"
    android:configure="expo.modules.widgetbridge.AccountsWidgetConfigActivity"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="1800000" />
